## What the inventory records

`scenes/inventory.md` holds 30 single-line rows, one per civic P2 row of
`docs/fantasy-world-scene-blueprints.tsv`. Each row records the source, the design note, the mockup
JPG, both shots, the MAPS rating, the MAPS note word for word from `docs/map-review.html`,
`judge: no`, `maker: Anthropic Sonnet`, and the state `inventoried`.

All 150 named paths were checked with `ls` and exist. All 30 briefs at
`bench/sonnet/briefs/map-p2-<slug>.md` exist. Four rows hold an empty MAPS note in the source page;
they read `none recorded`. No row holds `missing`, because all 30 sources exist.

## The replaced draft

The prior MiniMax run left an untracked draft. Row-by-row comparison with `docs/map-review.html`
showed that it altered 8 of 30 MAPS notes to remove the substring `rated`. Those notes say
"orchestrator rated 7.0"; the draft said "orchestrator scored 7.0". The eighth note says "mockup
generated after build"; the draft said "mockup created after build". That rewrites a recorded
source note, so this role replaced the draft with faithful text.

## Blocked state and the Red fix

On `8e20f73d` the checker could not exit 0. A9 scanned its own `$0` for the archive path literal,
which sits in its own source. P1-d ran a file-wide `grep -F "rated"`, which matched eight faithful
notes. Red fixed both in `e964238a`: A9 now tests the `TRACK_DIR` value, and P1-d reads the state
cell only. This role did not edit the checker.

